From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:21:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] editor erosion: droplet feedback rounds default 32 (4 gave
 lone grooves, no branching), stream power cut share F/(1+F) so k scales the
 cut, valley width grows with the catchment (width_vary), route_every, tests
 (TestFeedbackAndHierarchy, goldens)

The default droplet run refreshed its steering surface only 4 times, so droplets of one round never saw each other's gullies: a smear of worms on the plains,
soft cliffs, no branching. 32 rounds: gullies capture their neighbours, branch and leave sharp ridges (fine relief x3 on smooth hills, 48% of the samples dissected
instead of 2%). erode_stream: min(k * sqrt(area) * slope, max_cut * drop) sat at its cap for any k above ~0.1 (k 0.5 and 4 gave the same terrain); the share is now
F / (1 + F) with F = k * area^m. The incision is smoothed more for bigger catchments (integer thresholds, no libm) and the drainage network can be rebuilt every n steps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F37er45a7etRuMgEW1q3kY

